+## S3-CREDITS (2026-11-15): the credits parade, resident delta -48 B, pixels unchanged
+
+The GBA credits package (docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 3: S3-CREDITS") touches shared core code, so the PS1 was built and run on the tree
+before and after (`cmake --preset ps1 -DDOOMO_INTRO_REQUIRED=ON`, boot FMV, `PSN00BSDK_LIBS=/opt/psn00bsdk/lib/libpsn00b`): **129,504 ->
+129,456 B below the stack top** (-48 B resident: `look_run_hash` returns early when an id has no deep run, `cr_confetti_xy` and
+`cr_fans_xj` replace the closed forms with their divisions, the ticker's panel key and `ui_title_kept` are compiled out because
+`UI_PANELS` is 0; the SPEED share of 2 KB is untouched). The PS1 draws the parade exactly as before: `credits.c` sets
+`DoomoOverworldView.lite` but only the GBA reads it, and `PC_BODY_SPAN` is `#if`'d to the GBA (the PS1 keeps `PC_STANDIN` 4).
+Checked in PCSX-Redux with the credits windows of `speed2_story.txt` (`tools/speed2.py ps1`): the three screenshots (`story_cut_press`,
+`story_credits`, `story_credits_parade`) are byte-identical before and after; fps 29.89 -> 30.00 (credits, the one 67 ms frame
+stays in both) and 30.00 -> 30.00 (parade, one 50 ms frame both times). `game_smoke` PASS.
